  "_comment": "One table, two implementations: ouroboros.configured_subagents (subagent_handle, roster_handles, validate_unique_engines) and web/modules/route_editor_primitives.js (subagentHandle, rosterHandles, sameEngineAs). 'global_processing' is the inherited OUROBOROS_PROCESSING_PREFERENCE the roster is read under ('' when absent); 'handle' is a pure function of ONE row's EFFECTIVE facts with baselines (full access, standard processing) omitted; 'roster' is the label the live roster shows (twins get ~<stored id>); 'same_engine_as' is the index of the earlier row a save refuses this row against (null = accepted). 'snapshots' are frozen task snapshots and history identities (Python only: the browser never reads one) - a record is named from its OWN facts, so a pre-access snapshot is named by the workspace_write it actually ran with.",
